  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760331,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1999: A Commodore 64 Classic\n\nStep into the year 1999, a dystopian future where the world is ravaged by pollution and controlled by the oppressive Global Dominion. You are a young rebel, forced to flee your home after witnessing a brutal act of injustice. Your mission: to reach the legendary Free Zone and ignite a spark of hope against the Dominion's iron grip.\n\n*1999* masterfully blends text adventure, RPG, and arcade gameplay. Explore detailed locations, solve challenging puzzles through text commands, and engage in fast-paced, side-scrolling action sequences.  Develop your character's skills – strength, agility, and intelligence – to overcome obstacles and defeat the Dominion's robotic enforcers. \n\nThe game features a compelling narrative driven by your choices, multiple endings, and a haunting soundtrack that perfectly captures the bleak atmosphere.  Discover hidden secrets, uncover the truth behind the Dominion's rise to power, and ultimately decide the fate of humanity in this unforgettable Commodore 64 experience. Prepare for a journey of survival, rebellion, and hope in a world on the brink."
    },
